# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the nightly's ctest run (the linux-tsan test
# preset points TSAN_OPTIONS at this file; ADR-0013). Only known false
# positives belong here, never a race in our own code: fix that instead. Every
# entry says why it is here, above it.
#
# Format: https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/ThreadSanitizerSuppressions

# GameNetworkingSockets (ADR-0003) takes its global lock second, against its
# own lock order, only through a timed try-lock that backs off on timeout
# (SteamNetworkingGlobalLock::TryLock in its socket thread and Poll): that can't
# deadlock. TSan records the timed acquisition (pthread_mutex_clocklock) like a
# blocking one and reports a lock-order inversion. Only GameNetworkingSockets
# uses std::recursive_timed_mutex, and only timed acquisitions go through
# _M_clocklock, so nothing of ours matches.
deadlock:std::recursive_timed_mutex::_M_clocklock
